.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt MUSE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm muse
.Nd Meta's Muse Code, a coding agent for the terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar prompt
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
works on the files of the directory it starts in at a person's request: it
sends the request to a model of Meta's Model API, reads and edits files and
runs shell commands as the model asks, and shows the conversation on the
terminal.
With no command it opens its interactive screen;
.Ql muse exec Ar prompt
runs one request to the end without one.
.Ql muse --help
lists the options and commands, and
.Ql muse Ar command Fl -help
describes one.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=muse os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is Meta's own build of version 1.4.10-R6427.1 for Linux on
x86-64, a static executable, installed unmodified as Meta's release has it.
.Pa /opt/muse/bin/muse
is the program, and
.Pa /usr/bin/muse
and
.Pa /bin/muse
link to it.
Meta's installer also installs a launcher that updates the program; the
root does not have it.
Meta gives the program under its Model API Terms of Service, which forbid
modifying it or giving it to anyone else;
.Pa /opt/muse/TERMS
says so and gives their address.
.Pp
The first time
.Nm
opens its screen in a directory, it asks whether to trust it.
A trusted directory's own instructions, skills, rules and hooks are loaded,
and the answer is kept in
.Pa ~/.config/muse/trust.json .
.Ss Signing in over SSH
With no credential, the screen offers
.Dq Log in with browser
and
.Dq Set an API key .
The first prints an address at
.Lk https://auth.meta.com
with a one-time code, and tries to open it with
.Ql xdg-open ,
which the machine does not have.
Open the address on any other computer, sign in to Meta there and confirm
the code;
.Nm
waits for Meta's answer and then stores the session it is given.
.Ql muse login
does the same from the shell.
The second reads a Model API key, checks it with Meta and stores it;
.Ql muse auth set --api-key-stdin
stores one read from standard input.
A key in the environment variable
.Ev META_API_KEY
is used without signing in and is not stored, and it takes priority over a
stored key, which takes priority over a stored session.
.Ql muse logout
removes the stored credential.
.Ss Where the credential lives
.Nm
keeps a stored credential in
.Pa ~/.config/muse/auth.json ,
beside its settings in
.Pa ~/.config/muse/settings.json ;
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
followed by
.Pa /muse
names another directory.
Its sessions, their index and its logs are under
.Pa ~/.local/share/muse ,
or
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
followed by
.Pa /muse .
.Ss The sandbox
By default
.Nm
asks before a command with side effects and runs each shell command in a
sandbox, which on Linux is a copy of bubblewrap built into the program.
Bubblewrap needs parts of Linux that Rach2 does not have yet, among them
.Fn pivot_root ,
and Meta documents that
.Nm
refuses a shell command when it cannot run it in the sandbox.
.Fl -disable-sandbox
runs commands without it, and
.Fl -yolo
also turns off the approvals and trusts the directory, for one run.
.Ss Updates and telemetry
The program does not update itself; a new version comes with a new build
of the root.
A line of the settings file turns off its telemetry to Meta:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"schema_version": 1, "telemetry": {"enabled": false}}
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/muse/bin/muse
the program
.It Pa /opt/muse/TERMS
the terms it is used under
.It Pa ~/.config/muse/auth.json
the stored credential
.It Pa ~/.config/muse/settings.json
the settings
.It Pa ~/.config/muse/trust.json
the directories trusted or not
.It Pa ~/.local/share/muse
the sessions, their index and the logs
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, such as
.Ql muse exec
with no credential, and 2 for an option it does not know.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in, then work in a repository without the sandbox:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ muse login
$ cd project
$ muse --disable-sandbox
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gh 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1
.Pp
.Lk https://dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code "The Muse Code documentation"
